cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite both the original SCRAPS paper listed in references and the
  Zenodo DOI for the m_scraps release you used. The Zenodo DOI will be added
  to this file when the archive is available.
type: software
title: "m_scraps: multi-sublattice short-range-order and cluster-correlation targeting"
version: 0.5.0
authors:
  - family-names: Arróyave
    given-names: Raymundo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0773-9939"
    affiliation: Texas A&M University
repository-code: "https://github.com/rarroyave/m_scraps"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  m_scraps extends SCRAPS / Hybrid-Cuckoo-Search with per-pair short-range-order
  targets, independently constrained sublattices, decorated pair/triplet/quadruplet
  correlations, structure evaluation, and reproducible external-reference tests.
  Original SCRAPS authorship and licensing are preserved.
  Development of m_scraps is supported by the U.S. National Science Foundation
  under Award OAC-2608825 (PhaseForge).
keywords:
  - short-range order
  - special quasirandom structures
  - multi-sublattice alloys
  - ceramics
references:
  - type: article
    title: Accelerating computational modeling and design of high-entropy alloys
    authors:
      - {family-names: Singh, given-names: Rahul}
      - {family-names: Sharma, given-names: Aayush}
      - {family-names: Singh, given-names: Prashant}
      - {family-names: Balasubramanian, given-names: Ganesh}
      - {family-names: Johnson, given-names: Duane D.}
    journal: Nature Computational Science
    volume: 1
    start: 54
    end: 61
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.1038/s43588-020-00006-7
